  "boundary": "R-183 proves the exact finite 2x2 reserve criterion for the R-182 cross block under the registered beta=1/2 pullback: the original diagonal reserves p=d1-a and q=d2-a are sufficient when p>0 and q>=a^2/p, and the witness x=-a/p,y=1 makes this condition necessary for nonnegativity. In the isotropic case the exact threshold is d>=2a; with a=8 it is d>=16, while d=15 has a negative relative-phase fixture. This is a conditional finite margin theorem only. It does not identify the heat, forest, complement, returned-low, source or sextic terms with d1,d2, prove their production lower bounds, close T-050/A13, close Sector-A, compare physical-empty states, or establish removal, continuum, Nelson or measure results. No gate closure, tier change, new negative or PDF follows.",
